# Site-local desktop settings.
#
# This file exists so that the `local` database named in /etc/dconf/profile/user
# always compiles - dconf warns on every read if a profile references a database
# that has never been built.
#
# ROS does not ship anything here. Add your own keyfiles beside this one for
# settings that belong to this installation and should survive a ROS upgrade;
# they take precedence over the ROS defaults and are themselves overridden by
# anything the management console pushes.
